rue] [17592186673114 1083 #uuid "1045ca11-00a7-54f5-82df-d90677220306" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673115 1080 "false" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673115 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673115 1083 #uuid "14c0ef31-2044-5855-a7a9-cab2011298ac" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673116 1080 "III only" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673116 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673116 1083 #uuid "15b93aa7-c591-5841-aa3a-357d8bf16eef" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673117 1068 #edb/ref 17592186673145 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673117 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673117 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $\\operatorname{Col}(A)\\subsetneq\\mathbb{R}^{n}$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673117 1072 #uuid "24f7a599-64fa-59b0-bc94-5119ac1b11b5" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673117 1074 "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* ×\n\nEvery finite-dimensional subspace has a basis. The zero subspace has the empty basis.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{Col}(A)\\subsetneq\\mathbb{R}^{n}$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III only." 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673118 1080 "true" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673118 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673118 1083 #uuid "348adaf6-7787-565e-9ff4-1f701aa97384" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673119 1080 "false" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673119 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673119 1083 #uuid "3b0d39f6-4254-5d22-bf4e-6febe4ad2533" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673120 1080 "I and II only" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673120 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673120 1083 #uuid "4238513f-e322-530e-9565-e1ef6525b9d9" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673121 1080 "II and III only" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673121 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673121 1083 #uuid "45cde434-4d75-5c09-9b0f-35b920274076" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673122 1080 "I and III only" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673122 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673122 1083 #uuid "52405711-96a4-58b9-b20b-772647cc4c5b" 13194139538748 17592186045443 true] [17592186673123 1080 "false" 13194